# CODEOWNERS — automatic review assignment + required reviews.
# Later rules override earlier ones. Order: generic → specific.
# Combine with a branch ruleset: "Require review from Code Owners".
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# ⚠️  Every team named here must exist in the actana org, or GitHub silently
#     assigns nobody — and with "Require review from Code Owners" enabled, the
#     PR can then never be approved. Create @actana/maintainers before turning
#     that rule on. See docs/REPO_SETUP.md.
#
# One team on purpose: the template's backend/frontend/docs/platform split
# describes a layout this repo does not have (there is no /src, no /infra), and
# teams that do not exist are worse than no rule. The per-package lines below
# are where a split would go once there are enough maintainers to route.

# ---- Default owners for everything not matched below ----
*                           @actana/maintainers

# ---- The two halves of the product ----
/packages/panel/            @actana/maintainers
/packages/harness/          @actana/maintainers

# The wire contract both halves agree on. A change here is a compatibility
# event — the Panel and its Cores are version-locked — never a local edit.
/packages/shared/           @actana/maintainers

# ---- Protected: the decisions, the contracts, and the release path ----
/CONTEXT.md                 @actana/maintainers
/docs/adr/                  @actana/maintainers
/.github/                   @actana/maintainers
/SECURITY.md                @actana/maintainers
/LICENSE                    @actana/maintainers
/NOTICE                     @actana/maintainers
/Dockerfile                 @actana/maintainers
/install.sh                 @actana/maintainers
/deploy/                    @actana/maintainers
/package.json               @actana/maintainers
/pnpm-lock.yaml             @actana/maintainers
/pnpm-workspace.yaml        @actana/maintainers
